From 130921f5cc1404512e97407f627f472a47bb70e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 17:39:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] riscv: add Baochip bao1x SoC and Dabao board support

Add ARCH_BAOCHIP, the bao1x SoC devicetree (VexRiscv rv32imac with
Sv32, the external interrupt array + IRQARRAY fabric, uDMA serial/
I2C/SPI, IOX pinctrl and the RRAM with its partition layout), the
Dabao board devicetree (350MHz timebase from the emulated rdtime,
perclk fixed-clock, uDMA UART2 console) and a defconfig that carries
the 2MiB-RAM discipline this machine needs (XIP kernel at the RRAM
addresses, 4K stacks, no sysfs/block, 4K log buffer).

The CPU compatible is registered in the riscv cpus binding;
dtbs_check passes for the board.

Co-developed-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
